is call him up and say,

00:10:03.602 --> 00:10:06.805
"Uh, yeah. No, we're finding
a lot of stuff down here.

00:10:06.805 --> 00:10:08.307
No, no, no,
you wouldn't believe it.

00:10:08.307 --> 00:10:10.609
Hey, can I get another Mai Tai,
and this time can I get a,

00:10:10.609 --> 00:10:13.078
I don't know, inside a pineapple
with a little umbrella?

00:10:13.078 --> 00:10:14.546
Thank you.
Anyway, yeah, Donald.

00:10:14.546 --> 00:10:16.048
We're finding
lots of proof down here.

00:10:16.048 --> 00:10:19.117
We're going to need
some more money and maybe a...

00:10:19.117 --> 00:10:21.387
Maybe a masseuse?"
This is the same scam

00:10:21.387 --> 00:10:23.188
Trump's been running
for years, and every time

00:10:23.188 --> 00:10:24.924
Republicans and their voters
eat it up.

00:10:24.924 --> 00:10:28.160
For example, Trump actually went
through with that dumb threat

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:30.362
to investigate
voter fraud in 2016

00:10:30.362 --> 00:10:33.165
and put together a commission
that was so unsuccessful,

00:10:33.165 --> 00:10:36.201
they had to disband it
after finding nothing.

00:10:36.201 --> 00:10:37.736
The commission was led by
Kris Kobach,

00:10:37.736 --> 00:10:39.405
the former Kansas
Secretary of State,

00:10:39.405 --> 00:10:41.640
who found so little proof
of voter fraud,

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:44.810
he got humiliated in
a disastrous interview on CNN.

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:46.879
-We have about 3 million people

00:10:46.879 --> 00:10:48.614
who are registered
in more than one state,

00:10:48.614 --> 00:10:50.082
and that's not a crime.
-Right, including --

00:10:50.082 --> 00:10:51.316
-That's just an administrative
bookkeeping --

00:10:51.316 --> 00:10:52.651
-Including the president's
son-in-law,

00:10:52.651 --> 00:10:54.286
including the president's
Treasury Secretary.

00:10:54.286 --> 00:10:56.455
-Exactly.
Yeah, and many of your viewers

00:10:56.455 --> 00:10:58.190
are probably registered
in more than one state.

00:10:58.190 --> 00:11:00.759
But what is a crime is
if you actually vote

00:11:00.759 --> 00:11:02.961
in both of those states
or in more than two states.

00:11:02.961 --> 00:11:04.696
-Of course it's a crime.
-And every --

00:11:04.696 --> 00:11:06.898
-But where is the evidence
of this widespread,

00:11:06.898 --> 00:11:09.067
rampant
millions of people voting?

00:11:09.067 --> 00:11:12.104
If it had happened,
why haven't we seen it?

00:11:12.104 --> 00:11:13.972
-We've already filed nine cases.
-From the notes that I saw,

00:11:13.972 --> 00:11:15.875
you have nine cases.
-And we have six guilty pleas.

00:11:15.875 --> 00:11:18.243
-Right, six guilty pleas,
one dismissed,

00:11:18.243 --> 00:11:20.746
two pending --
that's as January 25th.

00:11:20.746 --> 00:11:25.084
Nine cases does not rampant
widespread voter fraud make.

00:11:25.084 --> 00:11:28.153
And -- and the nine cases
are just the ones

00:11:28.153 --> 00:11:29.455
at the top of the list.

00:11:29.455 --> 00:11:30.756
One of the interesting
things we found

00:11:30.756 --> 00:11:32.657
in prosecuting
this crime in Kansas

00:11:32.657 --> 00:11:35.494
is that both Republicans
and Democrats do it.

00:11:35.494 --> 00:11:37.129
-These guys are such
bumbling morons

00:11:37.129 --> 00:11:38.597
they went from claiming
that there were

00:11:38.597 --> 00:11:42.100
3 to 5 million illegal votes,
all of them for Democrats,

00:11:42.100 --> 00:11:43.702
to there were six guilty pleas

00:11:43.702 --> 00:11:45.204
and some of them were
Republicans.

00:11:45.204 --> 00:11:46.772
It's like an episode
of "Law &amp; Order" that starts

00:11:46.772 --> 00:11:48.473
with a jogger
finding a body in the park

00:11:48.473 --> 00:11:51.476
and ends with a coroner's report
that says, "He was just sleeping

00:11:51.476 --> 00:11:53.078
and now he's pissed
and he's a lawyer

00:11:53.078 --> 00:11:54.413
and he's suing us."

00:11:54.413 --> 00:11:55.614
There's a common through line

00:11:55.614 --> 00:11:57.716
from birtherism
to lies about voter fraud.

00:11:57.716 --> 00:11:59.852
Republicans
don't see their opponents

00:11:59.852 --> 00:12:02.021
as legitimate,
and they don't accept

00:12:02.021 --> 00:12:03.955
the outcomes
of democratic elections.

00:12:03.955 --> 00:12:05.891
That's why they claimed
the first black president

00:12:05.891 --> 00:12:07.159
wasn't born here

00:12:07.159 --> 00:12:09.127
and that mail ballots
are somehow fraudulent

00:12:09.127 --> 00:12:11.130
or that a secret army
of dead people rose up

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:12.898
from their graves,
voted in this election,

00:12:12.898 --> 00:12:14.333
and then held
a press conference

00:12:14.333 --> 00:12:15.634
in front
of a landscaping company.

00:12:15.634 --> 00:12:17.235
[ As Rudy ]
"Thanks for coming, everyone.

00:12:17.235 --> 00:12:18.503
It's getting late,
so I better scoot on over

00:12:18.503 --> 00:12:20.072
to the cremation center."

00:12:20.072 --> 00:12:21.874
The Republican Party's
an authoritarian movement

00:12:21.874 --> 00:12:24.143
that is opposed to democracy
and does not see victories

00:12:24.143 --> 00:12:25.911
by their political opponents
as legitimate.

00:12:25.911 --> 00:12:28.847
They believe they are
the only ones entitled

00:12:28.847 --> 00:12:31.984
to wield power regardless
of what voters actually want.

00:12:31.984 --> 00:12:33.886
Maybe it's just me,
but I'm not sure we can have

00:12:33.886 --> 00:12:36.621
a functioning democracy
if one side refuses to accept

00:12:36.621 --> 00:12:38.023
the results whenever they lose.

00:12:38.023 --> 00:12:41.193
And even if this specific
coup attempt doesn't work,

00:12:41.193 --> 00:12:43.295
that's not like good news.

00:12:43.295 --> 00:12:44.796
Someone tries to rob a bank

00:12:44.796 --> 00:12:46.732
but gives up because
he can't crack the safe,

00:12:46.732 --> 00:12:49.201
you install
new security measures

00:12:49.201 --> 00:12:50.636
to stop them
from doing it again.

00:12:50.636 --> 00:12:52.771
You don't just wave goodbye
and say "No harm, no foul.

00:12:52.771 --> 00:12:54.806
Take care, buddy.
Come back, you know,

00:12:54.806 --> 00:12:56.308
if you want to open
a checking account."

00:12:56.308 --> 00:12:57.610
Suffice to say,

00:12:57.610 --> 00:12:59.778
it's not a good situation
when you have

00:12:59.778 --> 00:13:01.880
one political party
committed to democracy

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:03.148
no matter the outcome,

00:13:03.148 --> 00:13:05.450
and the other opposed
to democracy at all costs.

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:07.520
Even if this ridiculous
coup attempt fails,

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:08.988
it doesn't bode well
for the future,

00:13:08.988 --> 00:13:11.990
which is why we need
bold systemic reforms

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:13.992
to empower everyone to vote
and honor

00:13:13.992 --> 00:13:15.861
what the majority
of voters actually want,

00:13:15.861 --> 00:13:17.563
like abolishing
the electoral college

00:13:17.563 --> 00:13:20.499
and fixing the Voting Rights
Act, among other things.

00:13:20.499 --> 00:13:22.267
These should be no-brainers.

00:13:22.267 --> 00:13:24.536
If we had a healthy
functioning political system,

00:13:24.536 --> 00:13:27.039
both parties would react to
these ideas by saying...

00:13:27.039 --> 00:13:28.239
-Sure, done.

00:13:28.239 --> 00:13:29.942
-This has been "A Closer Look."

